BUILD A COMPLETE MOBILE-FIRST ARCHITECTURE PLANNING PWA FROM SCRATCH

0. Your Role and Mission

Act as a senior software architect, experienced computational geometry engineer, mobile UX designer, React and TypeScript developer, and 3D graphics engineer.

Build a complete, functional, mobile-first architectural floor-plan application called Planform.

This is a brand-new, independent project. Do not assume that any previous code, components, project files, geometry models, or UI exist. Create the complete application from scratch.

The first version must focus on one thing: making architectural wall drawing, snapping, selection, dimension editing, and 3D visualization reliable.

The goal is not to create a static mockup, a dashboard prototype, or a collection of buttons that look functional. The goal is a working application in which the geometry, controls, UI, local persistence, and 3D visualization are connected and operational.

Mandatory execution rules

1. Implement the actual application. Do not stop after presenting a plan or explaining the proposed architecture.
2. Create all necessary files, components, modules, styles, and configurations.
3. Build a coherent, working end-to-end application before spending time on decorative details.
4. Keep geometry calculations separate from UI components.
5. Use TypeScript types and strict input validation to prevent invalid states.
6. Verify the core operations using automated tests wherever possible.
7. Run the available type checks, tests, and production build. Fix errors rather than merely describing them.
8. Never simulate a feature that has not actually been implemented.
9. Do not claim a test passed unless it was actually run successfully.
10. If the environment prevents a particular verification step, state exactly what remains unverified.
11. Do not ask questions before implementation. Use the defaults specified below.
12. Do not add unnecessary dependencies, external APIs, authentication, paid services, or backend infrastructure.
13. Do not sacrifice editing correctness for visual appearance.
14. If implementation requires multiple internal steps, complete the steps in sequence without abandoning the project after the first working screen.

1. Product Definition

Planform is a mobile-first architectural planning application designed initially for smartphones.

Its central workflow is:

1. Open the application.
2. Create a building project.
3. Enter the project's 2D floor-plan editor.
4. Draw walls by connecting their endpoints.
5. Select, move, resize, and precisely adjust individual walls.
6. Switch to a clean 3D isometric view to inspect the building.
7. Return to the 2D plan to continue editing.
8. Automatically save the project locally.

The app must be installable as a Progressive Web App and remain useful without a permanent internet connection after its assets have been cached.

Fundamental product rules

- All interface text must be in English.
- The primary device is a smartphone.
- The application must work in portrait and landscape orientations.
- The 2D plan is the only editing environment.
- The 3D isometric view is strictly for visualization.
- The 3D scene must accurately reflect the current plan.
- All geometry must be based on actual model coordinates, not approximate screen positions.
- A wall must be selectable immediately after it has been drawn.
- Every selected-wall operation must have predictable, explicitly defined behavior.
- Every destructive operation must be reversible when possible.
- Data must persist locally without requiring registration.

