Use IndexedDB for local project persistence, with versioned project records and safe initialization.

If IndexedDB is unavailable or inaccessible, fail gracefully and display a clear message rather than crashing the application.

Automatic saving

Automatically save project changes.

Show an understandable saving state, such as:

- Saving
- Saved
- Unable to Save

Use an appropriate debounce for frequent geometry updates, while ensuring committed edits are not lost.

Do not display Saved before the persistence operation has succeeded.

Handle concurrent save requests in a predictable order so an older save cannot overwrite newer geometry.

Update the project's last-modified date after relevant changes.

Project recovery

On application startup:

- Load existing projects.
- Validate their stored schemas.
- Recover valid data.
- Handle missing or malformed records gracefully.
- Never crash the entire application because one project record is invalid.

Use safe schema migrations if the data model changes.

Do not silently discard a project's data when a migration fails.

Import and export

Provide an option to export a project as a JSON backup.

Include the project metadata, points, walls, and schema version.

Provide an import function for compatible project JSON files.

Validate all imported data before saving or opening it.

Reject malformed files and explain the error in a readable way.

Do not overwrite an existing project with imported data without explicit confirmation.

Do not execute code contained in imported files.

Keep all project data local unless the user explicitly exports it.

